 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Pick a spot that's not under any trees or shrubs, on level ground if you can, and that's not right by the toilet. That's a classic mistake. Trees are great for shade, but they stretch far out at the base, pulling the ground down. That happens. Pull the tree from the tent if you can, and drive pegs into the ground around it. Avoid sleeping there if you can. The ground gets hot and the tent shades it, so things can catch fire. Exactly. And raise it on poles or sticks so it doesn't touch the ground.",
